# Septr's own Go SDK contains intentional attack payloads used to:
#   - self-test the engine (selftest.go, *_test.go)
#   - define detection patterns (ssrf.go, sanitize.go)
#   - exercise adapters with real attack payloads (gin.go, nethttp.go)
# These are NOT vulnerabilities — excluding them is intentional.

# Tests exercise the detectors with real attack payloads
**/*_test.go

# Self-test engine: fires every detector with representative payloads
selftest.go

# Detection pattern definitions — the attack strings ARE the product here
ssrf.go
sanitize.go

# Adapters embed self-test payloads inline
gin.go
nethttp.go
